subproblem.statement:
Let n, N, p ∈ ℕ, M ⊆ ℝ^N, θ : ℝ^N → ℝ, f : ℝ^N → ℝ^p, ψ : ℝⁿ → ℝ^N and u ∈ ℝⁿ. Put x := ψ(u), A := fderiv ℝ ψ u, T := range A and B := fderiv ℝ (f∘ψ) u. Assume:
- θ(x) ≠ 0;
- HasWeightedApproximateTangentSpaceAt n M θ x T;
- HasLineDerivAt ℝ f (B w) x (A w) for every w ∈ ℝⁿ.

Then:
(i) approxTangentPlane n M θ x = T;
(ii) there is a continuous linear L : T → ℝ^p with HasTangentialDifferentialAt T f x L;
(iii) areaJacobian (approxTangentPlane n M θ x) f x · normDet(A) = normDet(B).

Let n, N, p ∈ ℕ, ψ : ℝⁿ → ℝ^N, f : ℝ^N → ℝ^p, D ⊆ ℝⁿ, K, C ∈ ℝ≥0, J : ℝ^N → ℝ, S ⊆ ℝ^N and h : ℝ^N → [0, ∞]. Assume:
- D is compact;
- ψ is differentiable at every u ∈ D, and Dψ(u) is injective for u ∈ D;
- ψ is K-Lipschitz on D, and |u − v| ≤ C|ψ(u) − ψ(v)| for u, v ∈ D;
- f∘ψ is K-Lipschitz on D;
- S ⊆ ψ(D), and S is Hⁿ-measurable (null-measurable for μHE[n] on ℝ^N);
- for Lⁿ-a.e. u ∈ D with ψ(u) ∈ S, f∘ψ is differentiable at u and J(ψ(u))·normDet(Dψ(u)) = normDet(D(f∘ψ)(u));
- h is Hⁿ⌞S-a.e.-measurable.

Then ∫_S h·ofReal(J) dHⁿ = ∫_{ℝ^p} Σ_{x∈S∩f⁻¹{y}} h(x) dHⁿ(y), and y ↦ Σ_{x∈S∩f⁻¹{y}} h(x) is AEMeasurable for Hⁿ on ℝ^p.

Let X, Y be measurable spaces, μ, ν measures on X and Y, f : X → Y, g, h : X → [0, ∞], M ⊆ X and G : ℕ → Set X. For S ⊆ X put F_S(y) := Σ_{x∈S∩f⁻¹{y}} h(x). Assume:
- M and every G_α are μ-null-measurable;
- μ(M ∖ ⋃_α G_α) = 0 and ν(f(M ∖ ⋃_α G_α)) = 0;
- for every α and every μ-null-measurable S ⊆ M ∩ G_α, ∫_S g dμ = ∫ F_S dν and F_S is ν-AEMeasurable.

Then ∫_M g dμ = ∫ F_M dν.

Let n, N, p ∈ ℕ, M, U, N₀ ⊆ ℝ^N, (S_j)_{j∈ℕ} subsets of ℝ^N and f : ℝ^N → ℝ^p. Assume:
- U is open and M ⊆ U;
- f is locally Lipschitz on U;
- every S_j is an n-dimensional embedded C¹ submanifold of ℝ^N (IsC1Submanifold n (S j));
- M ⊆ N₀ ∪ ⋃_j S_j.

Then there are sets V_α, D_α ⊆ ℝⁿ, maps ψ_α : ℝⁿ → ℝ^N and constants K_α, C_α ∈ ℝ≥0 (α ∈ ℕ) such that M ⊆ N₀ ∪ ⋃_α ψ_α(D_α), and for every α:
- V_α is open, ψ_α is C¹ on V_α, and Dψ_α(u) is injective for all u ∈ V_α;
- D_α is compact and D_α ⊆ V_α;
- ψ_α is K_α-Lipschitz on D_α, and |u − v| ≤ C_α·|ψ_α(u) − ψ_α(v)| for all u, v ∈ D_α;
- f∘ψ_α is K_α-Lipschitz on D_α.

Let N, P, n ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^N, Z ⊆ ℝ^N and f : ℝ^N → ℝ^P, where ℝ^d = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d). Assume:
- f is locally Lipschitz on U: every x ∈ U has a neighbourhood t ∈ 𝓝[U] x on which f is Lipschitz;
- Z ⊆ U;
- Hⁿ(Z) = 0, where Hⁿ = μHE[n] is the n-dimensional Euclidean Hausdorff outer measure.

Then Hⁿ(f(Z)) = 0 in ℝ^P.
